summary:
The factorial of a number was implemented using two different methods:
iterative and recursive:
In the iterative method, a for loop is used to multiply numbers from 1 to n.
In the recursive method, the function repeatedly calls itself until it reaches the base condition.
For the given input 5, both methods produce the result 120.
The time complexity of both methods is O(n), while the iterative method requires less extra memory.

Conclusion

The implementation shows that both iterative and recursive methods can be used to calculate the factorial of a number effectively.
Although both have O(n) time complexity, the iterative method is more memory-efficient with O(1) space complexity, whereas the recursive method uses O(n) space because of recursive function calls.
Therefore, the iterative method is generally preferred when memory efficiency is important.
